<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    ONE CARD, THREE SECTIONS. 2026-08-25. POST-destructive deletions.

    STATUS: PREPARED, NOT AUTHORISED FOR DEPLOY. This file only DESCRIBES
    deletions; it performs nothing on its own.

    DELETES EXACTLY TWO COMPONENTS, both LightningComponentBundles that shipped
    this morning and lived for a few hours:

    1. bovPreferredBrokerCard
       The standalone "Preferred Broker" sidebar card. Its content is now SECTION
       1 of c/dispositionBuyerTimeline, which mounts the same c/bovPreferredBroker
       hero panel this card mounted. Nothing was rewritten; the lightning-card
       chrome around it was dropped.

    2. bovResponsesCard
       The standalone "BOV (n)" sidebar card. Its table markup, its CSS and its
       three-state visibility rule (rows / nothing / failed read) are now SECTION
       3 of the same bundle, under the dbt-bov-* class prefix. Its one behavioural
       change on the way across is the user's: the Broker Name column names the
       CONTACT rather than the firm, and only ONE row may read "Selected".

    WHY POST AND NOT PRE
    ====================
    package.xml in this same directory removes both componentInstances from
    flexipages/Disposition_Record_Page. That page edit must be LIVE BEFORE these
    bundles go: a FlexiPage referencing a deleted LightningComponentBundle does
    not deploy, and a bundle still referenced by a live page cannot be deleted.
    POST ordering satisfies both in one transaction. Validating this file in
    isolation gives a FALSE "still referenced" failure, because a destructive-only
    payload diffs against live org state where the page still names them - the
    ordering claim is only provable by a combined manifest + post destructive run.

    NOT IN SCOPE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE
    ====================================
      * bovPreferredBroker  SURVIVES. It is the hero PANEL, not the card, and it
        is mounted by both c/bovBrokerPanel (BOV Outreach) and now
        c/dispositionBuyerTimeline. Deleting it breaks two surfaces. The bundle
        names are one word apart; read them twice.
      * bovBrokerChangeHistory  SURVIVES, unchanged and unmoved. It was never part
        of this merge.
      * No Apex is deleted. BovController.getSubmissions is still read by
        c/bovBrokerPanel, c/bovComparisonMatrix and now the timeline.

    HOW TO RUN IT (only once authorised, and only alongside this folder's
    package.xml in the SAME command)
    ================================
      sf project deploy start
        with the manifest flag                 pointing at package.xml here
        with the post destructive changes flag pointing at this file
        with the target org flag               set to usman&#45;dpeg
    The flag prefixes are spelled out in words on purpose: an XML comment body
    cannot contain two consecutive hyphens.

    Do NOT pass the purge on delete flag; the bundles are recoverable from git
    history in any case.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>bovPreferredBrokerCard</members>
        <members>bovResponsesCard</members>
        <name>LightningComponentBundle</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
